{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Write batches of records in TraffluentCollector’s ingest format, for an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" to send,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and read them back into records on a server."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/collectorencoding"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"topicSections":[{"title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatch"],"anchor":"Encoding-batches"},{"title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorEncodingError"],"anchor":"Records-left-out"},{"title":"Decoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchDecoder","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/DecodedCollectorBatch","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchDecoderError","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/NotACollectorBatch"],"anchor":"Decoding-batches"},{"title":"Records that can’t be read","identifiers":["doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/UndecodedRecord","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorDecodingError"],"anchor":"Records-that-cant-be-read"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is the ","type":"text"},{"code":"BatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a self-hosted TraffluentCollector’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST \/v1\/batches","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Give it to an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") as its encoder,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and pass the collector’s API key to the destination as an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Authorization: Bearer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" header field.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is JSON: one object per record, with the record’s identifier (which a redelivered record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps), the event’s name, its timestamp, whether it is redelivered, its properties and its context.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Properties are read from the event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" form, which ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" derives, through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the encoder is made with. The context holds the standard","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context keys the record has values for, its session and sample rate, and its trace context. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value is written only while the record reveals it; once redacted, a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property is left out, and an array’s element, or a value inside a type the plan can’t map, is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one whose event and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"version the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event isn’t ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"text":", one holding a value","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"JSON can’t, such as a NaN, and one whose timestamp has no ISO 8601 form (NaN, infinite, or more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int64.max"},{"text":" milliseconds from 1970). ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true},{"text":" returns each record left out","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true},{"text":"), which the destination logs and reports on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"text":". When no record of a batch can be written, the destination sends nothing.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder\/batch(of:)","isActive":true},{"text":" returns the same body and skipped records without a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to a server of your own format, write a ","type":"text"},{"code":"BatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of your own. To send to PostHog,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"use ","type":"text"},{"code":"PostHogBatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"code":"PostHogEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import CollectorEncoding","import HTTPDestinations","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let encoder = CollectorBatchEncoder(plan: plan)","let collector = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: collectorURL,  \/\/ https:\/\/collector.example.com\/v1\/batches","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(apiKey)\"],","    encoder: encoder)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: collector)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers sending to the collector beside the other destinations."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Reading batches back","anchor":"Reading-batches-back"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchDecoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" reads a body the encoder wrote back into ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord"},{"text":"s, for a server","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that receives an app’s batches and hands them to another destination, such as a relay in front","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of Google Analytics. Make it with the plan the app’s encoder was made with. It finds each record’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event type by name among the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"text":"s the server links, or among the types you list","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchDecoder\/init(plan:events:instrument:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import CollectorEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let decoder = try CollectorBatchDecoder(plan: plan)","let batch = try decoder.batch(from: body)  \/\/ a body CollectorBatchEncoder wrote","await destination.receive(batch.records)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each record keeps its identifier, timestamp (to the millisecond), event, redelivery flag and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context the body holds: its session’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"text":", its sample rate, the standard context and its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trace context, which the decoder’s instrument extracts. Encoding the records again with an encoder","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the same plan writes the same bytes. A record the decoder can’t read is left out and the rest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are read: one of an event it has no type of, or whose type’s version the plan doesn’t describe, one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"missing a member or holding what the encoder never writes, and one with a property the event’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type can’t read: a required ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" property a delivery redacted, an array of non-optional","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" elements it redacted, or an integer outside its property’s type.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The body names each record’s event but not its version, so a record is read at the version of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"decoder’s type of that name. Deploy the server with the event types the apps send. Once an event’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"version is raised, a record from an app still at the earlier version is read as the newer one:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reported as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"undecodableProperty"},{"type":"text","text":" when its properties don’t fit the newer type, and read as the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"newer version when they do."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/DecodedCollectorBatch\/undecodedRecords","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" holds a report of each, an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/UndecodedRecord","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reason is a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorDecodingError","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". A body that isn’t a collector batch at all throws"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/NotACollectorBatch","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","title":"CollectorEncoding","externalID":"CollectorEncoding","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","modules":[{"name":"CollectorEncoding"}]},"references":{"doc://CollectorEncoding/documentation/CollectorEncoding/CollectorDecodingError":{"title":"CollectorDecodingError","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CollectorDecodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorDecodingError","url":"\/documentation\/collectorencoding\/